WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.810
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:02.970
happening all the time,

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.980
so we gathered some of
the most hyped products

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.260
from September to test for ourselves.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.570
I did it! I got my hands
on Clinique Black Honey.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.653
Never did I imagine

00:00:11.653 --> 00:00:13.228
a lipstick my mom wore back in the day

00:00:13.228 --> 00:00:16.110
would go viral in 2021, but here we are.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.350
This is a sheer lipstick-lip gloss hybrid

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.810
that has this just-bitten pink tint to it.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:22.590
It supposedly looks great on everyone

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.770
because it blends with
your natural lip tone.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.460
I really love this.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.135
I feel like you can get the same effect

00:00:28.135 --> 00:00:30.172
with one of those Burt's
Bee's tinted Chapsticks

00:00:30.172 --> 00:00:32.397
at the drugstore that are, like, $5,

00:00:32.397 --> 00:00:34.030
but the color of this is super beautiful,

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.420
and the formula is so
comfortable on the lips.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.610
It's hydrating and has a nice slip to it.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.650
About-Face is Halsey's makeup brand.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.190
It just dropped these two new products,

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.760
the Fractal Glitter Eye Paint

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.990
and the Fractal Glitter Brow Gel.

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.760
Let's talk about the eye paint first.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.520
I thought this packaging
was very cool and new,

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.210
like something I haven't seen before.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.310
I don't know. It seemed fun.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.790
And I love the color options
with these eye paints.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.290
It was a good mix of neutrals

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.990
and more exciting colors.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.930
I was worried these would dry quickly,

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.460
but I actually had no trouble

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.080
applying and blending them out.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.670
They didn't get streaky or patchy,

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.462
but I will say the bolder colors,

00:01:07.462 --> 00:01:08.611
like this blue one,

00:01:08.611 --> 00:01:11.130
do need a second layer for full coverage.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.510
If you're a one-and-done-
eye-shadow kind of person,

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.235
I think you'll like these.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:19.130
Now let's talk about
the glitter brow gels.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.360
Listen, I'm not going to pretend

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.960
that I'm interested in glitter brows,

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.410
but the products seem fun,

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.210
and I am interested in fun.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.480
I'm actually obsessed
with the brush on this.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.260
I really like how the
bristles brushed my brows.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.200
However, it does deposit
a bit too much product.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.410
You can see where I kind
of went outside the lines.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.340
The actual glitter effect is cute,

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.760
if you're into that sort of thing.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.930
I rubbed my brows to see

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.690
what the transfer situation is like,

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:44.560
and, surprisingly, the
hair seemed to stay put

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.980
and barely any glitter came off,

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.054
so I think the gel part of this product

00:01:48.054 --> 00:01:49.137
works really well.

00:01:49.137 --> 00:01:50.961
I do think that both of these products

00:01:50.961 --> 00:01:53.244
are really overpriced for what they are,

00:01:53.244 --> 00:01:54.840
but overall, I'm into this brand,

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.350
and I'm actually really excited to see

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.700
what they come out with next.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.240
I feel like it's been
forever since we as a group

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.230
have been excited over a sponge,

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.610
and this one has been
getting amazing reviews.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:07.790
This is the Real Techniques
Miracle Airblend Sponge.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.370
I tried this wet and dry.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:11.450
It doesn't expand very
much when you wet it,

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.269
but I liked it both ways.

00:02:13.269 --> 00:02:16.580
I've never felt a sponge like this before.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.160
It's completely weightless and squishy,

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.250
and because it's so
squishy, you can actually

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:24.260
really get into all those
crevices of your face.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.920
I really love how my makeup
looked after using this.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.300
It just looked really seamlessly blended.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.030
I actually prefer this one way more

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:34.020
than the Real Techniques
original orange sponge.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.253
The Nanoblur Instant Skin-Blurring Cream

00:02:36.253 --> 00:02:37.761
was an experience.

00:02:37.761 --> 00:02:39.288
I think I saw a TikTok that said

00:02:39.288 --> 00:02:40.846
they use this on the set of "Euphoria"

00:02:40.846 --> 00:02:42.550
to get rid of shininess.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.747
So, it says you can use
it underneath makeup

00:02:44.747 --> 00:02:47.560
and on top of makeup that
hasn't been set with powder yet,

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.060
so I tried it both ways.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.670
It definitely mattifies,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.120
but it leaves, like, a
white powdery cast behind.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.330
I'm not sure if I put too much on or what.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.740
My makeup started bunching
up between my brows

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.727
when I was blending my
foundation on top of it,

00:03:00.727 --> 00:03:01.750
and it just looked bad.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.170
Then I tried blending in a
small amount on my forehead

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.490
because I had some shine there,

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.140
and I feel like it did a little something,

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.100
but not enough for me
to ever use this again.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.610
I just think it's too
matte on my bare skin

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.803
and pretty underwhelming on top of makeup,

00:03:14.803 --> 00:03:16.550
so, yeah, I don't like this.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.980
This is the weirdest
primer I've ever used.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.280
This is the Smith &amp; Cult

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.970
Untouched Skin Brightening
Foaming Face Primer.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.300
I definitely overdid it
on my first application.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.666
It wasn't blending in at all,

00:03:26.666 --> 00:03:28.391
so I had to reapply it.

00:03:28.391 --> 00:03:30.930
The foam actually feels
really nice on the skin,

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.650
and I swear it has, like,
this cooling sensation

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:34.960
that I really liked. It felt good.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.200
It's a nice first step to your makeup.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.205
It certainly does brighten.

00:03:39.205 --> 00:03:41.200
I looked like a Victorian ghost woman.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.690
I feel like this almost
lightened my foundation.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.469
I get that it's brightening,

00:03:45.469 --> 00:03:47.722
but I didn't think it
would make my foundation

00:03:47.722 --> 00:03:51.270
a shade lighter. I had
to mix in a deeper shade.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.945
I do think my makeup looked nice

00:03:52.945 --> 00:03:54.011
on top of this primer,

00:03:54.011 --> 00:03:56.292
but I'm just not into the
brightening aspect of it.

